WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.470
(shouting)
(ethereal music)

00:00:04.707 --> 00:00:05.572
- We're filming a sword fight

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.604
and I need a really cool shot to end it.

00:00:07.604 --> 00:00:10.084
And I wanna film something
I've never seen before

00:00:11.196 --> 00:00:12.996
with a camera mounted on the sword

00:00:13.405 --> 00:00:16.324
as it cuts off the bad
guy's head in slow motion.

00:00:16.324 --> 00:00:17.416
But before I can do that,

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.564
I need to figure out how to build it

00:00:19.564 --> 00:00:20.425
and then film it.

00:00:20.425 --> 00:00:21.925
Let's put a GoPro on a sword.

00:00:22.145 --> 00:00:23.653
GoPro, roll video.

00:00:23.653 --> 00:00:24.627
(camera beeps)

00:00:24.627 --> 00:00:26.179
Oh my god, it's rolling.

00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:27.572
GoPro, stop recording.

00:00:27.572 --> 00:00:28.748
The idea is that we have this, like,

00:00:28.748 --> 00:00:30.166
looking down at the blade, right?

00:00:30.166 --> 00:00:31.266
You can stick it to things.

00:00:32.743 --> 00:00:34.064
Okay, that looks pretty sweet.

00:00:34.064 --> 00:00:35.284
- We wanna make sure that the blade

00:00:35.284 --> 00:00:36.584
is leading the frame though.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.493
- [Wren] Oh, so like this.

00:00:37.754 --> 00:00:39.236
- So that we see the destruction.

00:00:39.236 --> 00:00:40.465
- [Wren] This looks pretty sweet.

00:00:40.465 --> 00:00:41.725
How's it look going this way?

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.226
- [Nick] That looks pretty cool.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.182
(Wren roars mildly)

00:00:45.182 --> 00:00:46.013
- And we have a few katanas,

00:00:46.104 --> 00:00:48.297
like, there's this one,
but this is aluminum.

00:00:48.297 --> 00:00:50.332
It's useless for actually
chopping something.

00:00:50.332 --> 00:00:52.578
We do have one steel-bladed sword.

00:00:52.578 --> 00:00:54.380
It's very dull, as you can see.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.551
(mimics flesh ripping)

00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:58.407
Niko does have a really
nice high-quality katana.

00:00:58.407 --> 00:00:59.827
Maybe he'll let us use it for this.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.080
- Uh,

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:03.720
I'm gonna say no.

00:01:04.279 --> 00:01:05.588
- (Sighs) Okay.

00:01:05.588 --> 00:01:06.928
- I'm sorry.
- Okay.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.222
Unfortunately, this will
have to be the sword we use.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.060
It's not ideal.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.514
Now our issue is how do we sharpen this?

00:01:12.751 --> 00:01:13.688
This is steel.

00:01:13.688 --> 00:01:15.741
What if we actually just
take a belt sander to it?

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:16.658
- Yeah, let's try it.
- It's either that

00:01:16.658 --> 00:01:18.065
or we don't do this video.

00:01:18.065 --> 00:01:20.898
(energetic music)

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.857
I mean, that's kinda working.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.400
- [Nick] Dude, if we
hit that with some smooth.

00:01:33.991 --> 00:01:35.031
- [Sam] May I test it?

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.440
It feels a little sharp.

00:01:39.857 --> 00:01:40.972
Oh!

00:01:40.972 --> 00:01:42.523
(group shouting)

00:01:42.523 --> 00:01:43.765
Not bad, not bad.

00:01:43.765 --> 00:01:45.166
- This is sword test number one

00:01:45.166 --> 00:01:46.366
with a mini watermelon.

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:52.696
(relaxed electronic music)

00:01:52.696 --> 00:01:54.038
That is officially sharp.

00:01:54.038 --> 00:01:55.158
Let's go look at the footage.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.560
- [Nick] How's the footage look?

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.100
- [Wren] It's cool, I guess.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:00.971
- [Nick] What do you mean,
"it's cool, I guess?"

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.900
- Well, it's like it's so fast.

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.439
(mimics whooshing)
Did you see it?

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:06.958
Way faster than we expected.

00:02:06.958 --> 00:02:09.123
If I go through frame by frame,

00:02:09.123 --> 00:02:12.628
we now see the watermelon and the cut.

00:02:12.628 --> 00:02:14.786
There's way too much motion blur.

00:02:14.786 --> 00:02:17.841
Even though that we're recording
at 120 frames per second,

00:02:17.841 --> 00:02:20.535
the motion blur is so intense.

00:02:20.535 --> 00:02:23.477
(sighs) We wanna have as
little motion blur as possible,

00:02:23.477 --> 00:02:25.763
which means we have to have
a very high shutter speed,

00:02:25.763 --> 00:02:27.794
which means we need to
have a lot of light.

00:02:27.794 --> 00:02:28.803
We can go up to the roof,

00:02:28.803 --> 00:02:30.593
where we actually get
more direct sunlight.

00:02:30.593 --> 00:02:32.656
That should, in theory,
provide enough light

00:02:32.656 --> 00:02:35.165
so that the shutter speed
doesn't have to be dropped.

00:02:35.165 --> 00:02:36.340
- [Nick] Let's go check it out.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:38.014
- [Wren] Dude, yeah, so far,

00:02:38.014 --> 00:02:40.054
the motion blur, there's none.

00:02:40.657 --> 00:02:42.237
I mean, that was a good test right there.

00:02:42.237 --> 00:02:43.780
No motion blur.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:44.785
- [Nick] What?

00:02:44.785 --> 00:02:47.783
- Well, I mean, 100%
chance of rain tomorrow.

00:02:47.783 --> 00:02:48.730
- [Nick] Dang it!

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:49.655
- This is gonna be something that we just

00:02:49.655 --> 00:02:51.243
have to play by ear.

00:02:51.243 --> 00:02:52.410
Play by sight.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.193
I got it.

00:02:58.192 --> 00:02:59.621
Get the GoPro on.

00:02:59.621 --> 00:03:01.801
(camera beeping)
(water gurgling)

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.441
Okay, ready?

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.688
- [Nick] I think I'm ready.

00:03:04.698 --> 00:03:05.662
- Okay, I'm gonna wait
for that to come around

00:03:05.662 --> 00:03:07.046
and then I'm gonna slice through.

00:03:07.046 --> 00:03:08.211
Okay, ready?

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:08.800
- [Nick] Go for it.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:09.720
(Wren shouting)

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.920
(relaxed electronic music)

00:03:18.169 --> 00:03:19.349
(Wren grunting)

00:03:21.881 --> 00:03:23.979
- There are now to GoPros on this sword

00:03:23.979 --> 00:03:27.079
and we're gonna get both
angles at the same time.

00:03:28.831 --> 00:03:30.631
Alright, this is it, this is the cut.

00:03:31.704 --> 00:03:35.671
(Wren mimics whooshing)
(group shouting)

00:03:35.671 --> 00:03:37.765
I needed to have the
camera more angled though.

00:03:37.765 --> 00:03:38.748
(groans)

00:03:38.748 --> 00:03:40.261
What we learned is that

00:03:40.261 --> 00:03:41.794
this looks pretty sweet in slow motion,

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.160
but the camera placement
could have been way better.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:45.906
- Show me what you got.

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:47.723
(Sam mimics slow whooshing)

00:03:47.723 --> 00:03:49.515
That looks so cool.

00:03:49.515 --> 00:03:50.975
All those little flecks of paint,

00:03:50.975 --> 00:03:53.235
like, that looks so cool.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.461
And seeing the juice go (mimics warping).

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.225
Yeah, if you put the sword over there,

00:03:58.225 --> 00:03:59.053
on the left side of frame,

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.965
suddenly, all that chopping action

00:04:00.965 --> 00:04:02.486
is gonna be in the shot now.

00:04:02.486 --> 00:04:03.352
- Right, I have an idea.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.821
So we have two GoPros,

00:04:04.902 --> 00:04:06.379
one is Corridor's, one is Nick's.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:07.426
So here's the blade.

00:04:07.426 --> 00:04:09.732
We have one GoPro here
looking down the blade

00:04:09.732 --> 00:04:11.512
and then we take the second GoPro

00:04:11.512 --> 00:04:14.363
and put it straight up
horizontal along the blade.

00:04:14.363 --> 00:04:16.965
And this one will see all
of the debris that flies out

00:04:16.965 --> 00:04:19.055
and the other GoPro will see the cut.

00:04:19.055 --> 00:04:20.680
(gasps) And then what if we can somehow

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.778
stitch those shots together
for a super wide shot?

00:04:22.778 --> 00:04:23.806
That's a little high level.

00:04:23.806 --> 00:04:25.670
I don't know if I can do that.

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:26.615
That would be cool though.

00:04:26.615 --> 00:04:27.840
We might have a bit of stitch mark,

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:28.960
but that wouldn't,

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.322
I mean, if it's janky, embrace the jank.

00:04:31.322 --> 00:04:32.845
It is what it is.

00:04:32.845 --> 00:04:35.243
- I came in today to
find that Nick and Wren

00:04:35.243 --> 00:04:36.354
hadn't gotten the footage

00:04:36.354 --> 00:04:38.007
that they were looking for yesterday

00:04:38.007 --> 00:04:39.922
and, apparently, they've been
working on this video now

00:04:39.922 --> 00:04:41.428
for two or three days.

00:04:41.428 --> 00:04:43.119
This is the last day to get the footage

00:04:43.119 --> 00:04:45.908
that they need to get in
order to make this video cool

00:04:45.908 --> 00:04:48.040
or we're scrapping this whole project.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.767
- So I'm trying to line
these up so that I have

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:52.249
the right 25% of this camera matching up

00:04:52.249 --> 00:04:54.685
with the left 25% of this other camera

00:04:54.685 --> 00:04:56.925
so that I can have them overlapping.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.786
I'm gonna shoot, you ready?

00:04:59.786 --> 00:05:01.006
- [Nick] Go for it.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:05.280
(relaxed electronic music)

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.033
- Hey!

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:17.902
Nick, not bad.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:18.992
I think that turned out well.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.520
One, maybe two more and then
we go check the footage.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:24.480
I don't know, man.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:25.738
It's gonna be weird.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.340
The stuff in the distance
lines up really nicely

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.515
but stuff right next to the cameras,

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:31.090
they don't match up quite as nicely.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.318
The way we fix this is by
trying to get the lenses

00:05:34.515 --> 00:05:37.535
as close to each other
as physically possible.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:38.613
Like this.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:40.035
So I'm just gonna create a couple, like,

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.017
super, super small wood things

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:43.280
to help support this.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:47.262
So now I made a bit of a wedge.

00:05:47.262 --> 00:05:48.143
It's not perfect or anything,

00:05:48.143 --> 00:05:49.780
but hopefully it'll get the job done.

00:05:49.936 --> 00:05:51.446
A very, very dumb thing I'm about to do.

00:05:51.446 --> 00:05:53.191
Hey, hey, Carmichael.

00:05:53.191 --> 00:05:54.798
- [Nick] You're right in
time for the dumb thing.

00:05:54.798 --> 00:05:55.856
- Always am.

00:05:55.856 --> 00:05:58.466
- I am hot gluing this
piece of wood to the GoPro.

00:05:58.466 --> 00:06:02.686
Alright, so here is the final alignment.

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:05.355
At this point, we just
gotta get this thing filming

00:06:05.355 --> 00:06:06.535
'cause we're gonna be losing light.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:09.440
(tense music)

00:06:09.995 --> 00:06:11.735
- [Nick] Wren, we have
15 minutes to shoot.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:13.149
- Dear god, man!

00:06:13.358 --> 00:06:14.484
- [Nick] No!

00:06:14.484 --> 00:06:15.317
Hold on, GoPro.

00:06:15.317 --> 00:06:16.900
No, Wren, my GoPro!

00:06:18.149 --> 00:06:19.142
- Sorry, Nick.

00:06:19.142 --> 00:06:20.650
- [Nick] Franken-mount, dude.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:22.010
- Franken-mount.

00:06:22.587 --> 00:06:23.743
(groans) Okay.

00:06:23.743 --> 00:06:26.458
We are running out of time.

00:06:26.458 --> 00:06:28.798
- [Nick] Don't run with the sword, Wren!

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:29.813
God.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:32.893
(tense music)

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.340
- GoPro, record video.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.460
Alright, they are both rolling now.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:38.293
Here goes.

00:06:42.136 --> 00:06:43.536
- [Nick] That's what I'm talking 'bout.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.790
- I am not a samurai!

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.380
This is not ideal!

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.900
Well, we have now officially
chopped everything we have.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.948
This was our little 15-minute GoPro rig.

00:06:56.948 --> 00:06:59.188
We are just in time,
we're about to lose light.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:01.594
So hopefully, we still have enough

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.218
so that the background
isn't motion blurred.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.286
(grunts)

00:07:05.431 --> 00:07:06.264
So we got what we got

00:07:06.264 --> 00:07:07.478
and if it doesn't work, it doesn't work.

00:07:07.478 --> 00:07:08.639
It is what it is.

00:07:08.639 --> 00:07:09.979
Let's go look at the footage.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.039
- So these guys have been rolling

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:15.261
on swords cutting through
fruit for about a week now.

00:07:15.388 --> 00:07:16.651
And we're gonna finally
get to see the footage.

00:07:16.651 --> 00:07:17.631
I am super excited.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:19.669
- Okay, so this is the first rig

00:07:19.949 --> 00:07:21.828
where it was just the
regular mounts and cameras.

00:07:21.828 --> 00:07:23.275
(group chuckling)

00:07:23.275 --> 00:07:24.720
- [Man] Oh, on the drill.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:25.677
(mimics slashing)

00:07:25.677 --> 00:07:26.510
That's sweet.

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:27.343
- [Man] Oh, that's nice.

00:07:27.343 --> 00:07:28.240
- [Man] Did you spin all the way around

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.897
and hit it a second time?

00:07:29.897 --> 00:07:30.730
- Those are cool.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:31.714
That stuff's sweet.

00:07:31.714 --> 00:07:33.291
- That's really cool.
- That's cool.

00:07:33.291 --> 00:07:37.458
- [Man] This oddly reminds me
of Fruit Ninja, the VR game.

00:07:38.323 --> 00:07:40.029
- [Wren] This is essentially
1000 frames a second.

00:07:40.029 --> 00:07:40.862
- [Man] Interpolation?

00:07:40.862 --> 00:07:42.781
- (Groans) You didn't make it through!

00:07:42.781 --> 00:07:44.333
- I was just, I just
did like, the half thing

00:07:44.333 --> 00:07:45.854
'cause I was like, oh,
I've been going too fast.

00:07:45.854 --> 00:07:46.954
I'll go slower and then it was like

00:07:46.954 --> 00:07:47.843
it didn't make it through!

00:07:47.843 --> 00:07:48.676
It was like no!

00:07:48.676 --> 00:07:50.748
So the second rig was the super janky one,

00:07:50.748 --> 00:07:51.704
but it still works.

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:52.539
Check it out.

00:07:52.539 --> 00:07:54.911
So here is it without any blending.

00:07:54.911 --> 00:07:56.531
Just the two frames lined up.

00:07:57.552 --> 00:07:59.401
- Oops.
- And the sword actually bent

00:07:59.401 --> 00:08:00.674
a whole lot on that shot.

00:08:00.674 --> 00:08:02.614
(Niko laughing)

00:08:03.884 --> 00:08:05.366
(mimics whooshing)
- [Sam] That one looks like--

00:08:05.366 --> 00:08:08.092
- [Niko] This is like the
modern cubist, like, drawings.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.580
- Oh yeah, there we go.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.130
That somehow ended up being

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.198
one of the coolest things so far.

00:08:14.754 --> 00:08:15.776
- So here's the blended shot

00:08:15.776 --> 00:08:17.548
where I did, like, the repeat edges stuff,

00:08:17.548 --> 00:08:18.908
and, like, a feathered mask.

00:08:20.019 --> 00:08:22.221
Just to kind of try to
get some semblance of--

00:08:22.221 --> 00:08:23.144
- [Sam] Yeah, that was
a little gnarly there.

00:08:23.146 --> 00:08:23.979
- [Niko] It looks like you need to sharpen

00:08:23.979 --> 00:08:24.812
your sword a little bit.

00:08:24.812 --> 00:08:25.789
- [Niko] Oh!

00:08:25.789 --> 00:08:27.014
- [Wren] No, what happened
is that it got deflected

00:08:27.014 --> 00:08:29.824
and it was wanting to go up
while I was still pulling it.

00:08:29.824 --> 00:08:30.810
It was too sharp.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.198
That was the issue.

00:08:32.198 --> 00:08:33.985
- Wren, Nick, that turned out really good.

00:08:33.985 --> 00:08:37.459
That would be the ultimate
fatality shot in a sword fight.

00:08:37.459 --> 00:08:38.622
- Guys.
- Yes?

00:08:38.622 --> 00:08:39.982
- You're not fired anymore.

00:08:41.263 --> 00:08:42.779
Congratulations.

00:08:42.779 --> 00:08:46.362
(relaxed electronic music)

00:09:00.908 --> 00:09:02.908
♫ Do it

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:54.366
- [Niko] Three, two, one!

00:09:54.366 --> 00:09:56.669
(explosion)

00:09:56.669 --> 00:09:58.217
(group shouting)

00:09:58.217 --> 00:09:59.201
- Holy!

00:09:59.201 --> 00:10:00.201
- Oh my god!

00:10:02.069 --> 00:10:02.902
- Still rolling.
- Oh man.

